   "questionText": "Which processes consume the most manual effort (FTEs or hours per week) and are highly repetitive?",
   "answerText": "The most time-consuming and repetitive processes are typically:\n\nManual data entry and transferring information between systems\nProduction reporting and updating spreadsheets\nVisual quality inspections\nMaterial handling, sorting, packing, and palletizing\nInventory counting and stock reconciliation\nPreparing recurring reports and documentation\nManually recording downtime and maintenance activities\n\nThese processes should be measured by the number of employees involved and the total hours spent per week to identify the strongest automation opportunities.",
