   "category": "operations",
   "questionText": "How mature is your demand and capacity planning process?",
   "answerText": "Demand planning is monthly and spreadsheet-based, run by one planner with a long memory and no documented method. Capacity is checked against the same spreadsheet rather than against the actual available machine hours, so a plan that looks feasible on paper regularly loses the planned maintenance window when the order book tightens. Roughly nine hours a month of protected maintenance on Line 3 is released this way, and nobody records that it happened.",
   "isRequired": true,
