   "category": "operations",
   "questionText": "What are the most frequent causes of unplanned downtime or production disruption?",
   "answerText": "The visible causes are tooling failures and shuttle stoppages, which is what reaches the maintenance log. The measured reality is different: three quarters of the lost availability on Line 3 comes from stops shorter than four minutes, cleared by the operator at the machine and never logged. The controller data shows hundreds of them per week. Until the short-stop count is a reported number, the improvement effort will keep going to the wrong causes.",
