   "sessionId": "6174a0c0-8bf7-4244-98ba-7c4b8591c2d2",
   "category": "operations",
   "questionText": "How do you track and manage quality issues from detection through to root cause resolution?",
   "answerText": "Detection is good and traceability is incomplete. Nonconformances are raised at goods-in and in-process, and the quality tracker holds them through to closure. The chain breaks at Wakefield, where the paper checklist is re-keyed the following morning, so a batch received on Monday afternoon is not traceable until Tuesday. Supplier scoring is quarterly on a spreadsheet, which means a supplier whose quality starts slipping is visible a month after the fact.",
